{"id":84,"course_id":21,"title":"30-Day Interview Prep Operating Plan","summary":"Run job search like an incident response and learning system.","sequence":4,"body":"## Mental model\nA strong 30-day plan balances applications, networking, daily drills, mock interviews, hands-on labs, resume iteration, rest, and feedback loops. Track leading indicators so the search does not become a fog.\n\n## What to practice\nPractice scheduling blocks for Kubernetes debugging, Terraform plan review, AWS/IAM, CI/CD design, SRE incidents, behavioral stories, and company-specific prep.\n\n## Practice checkpoint\nBuild a 30-day tracker with target roles, study blocks, completed labs, mock results, applications, referrals, follow-ups, weak areas, and next actions.\n\n## Operator habit\nWrite down the symptom, the evidence, the suspected owner, and the safest next command before changing any live object. This turns scattered platform knowledge into a repeatable engineering workflow.","practice_notes":"Scenario: You are the platform engineer on call for a realistic team environment.\nChecklist:\n- State the user impact in one sentence.\n- Identify the system boundary and owner.\n- Collect read-only evidence first.\n- Propose the smallest reversible change.\n- Capture what should become a dashboard, alert, runbook, or automation.\nCommands:\n$ kubectl get events -A --sort-by=.lastTimestamp\n$ kubectl describe pod POD_NAME -n NAMESPACE\n$ kubectl logs deploy/APP -n NAMESPACE --since=15m","audio_url":null,"video_url":null,"course_slug":"platform-career-job-search-sprint","course_category":"Career","course_era":"Platform Academy","terms":[{"id":416,"term":"Platform Engineering Job Search Sprint","context":"Career","definition":"Turn learning into interview-ready proof: skill gap maps, portfolio narratives, resume bullets, recruiter screens, STAR stories, and a 30-day prep operating plan."},{"id":417,"term":"Evidence","context":"Debugging","definition":"Observed facts from commands, dashboards, logs, traces, events, or cloud APIs."},{"id":418,"term":"Blast radius","context":"Reliability","definition":"The set of users, tenants, workloads, or systems affected by a failure or change."},{"id":419,"term":"Rollback","context":"Operations","definition":"A planned path to return to a known-good state when a change causes harm."},{"id":420,"term":"Runbook","context":"Operations","definition":"A step-by-step guide that helps responders diagnose and mitigate an incident safely."}],"flashcards":[{"id":250,"lesson_id":84,"prompt":"What is the main goal of 30-Day Interview Prep Operating Plan?","answer":"Run job search like an incident response and learning system.","hint":"platform","difficulty":"beginner"},{"id":251,"lesson_id":84,"prompt":"Why collect evidence before changing live systems?","answer":"It reduces guessing, protects users, and makes the fix reviewable.","hint":"platform","difficulty":"beginner"},{"id":252,"lesson_id":84,"prompt":"What should a learner produce after each lab?","answer":"A clear diagnosis, a safe action plan, and a reusable note for future incidents.","hint":"platform","difficulty":"beginner"}]}
